---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import VenueCard from '../../components/VenueCard.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../../components/NewsletterBlock.astro';
import { routeSlug } from '../../lib/editorial';

const allVenues = await getCollection('venues');
const slugs = [
  'blue-moon-cottages',
  'mp-beach-club-cottages',
  'birch-creek',
  'kanasta-retro-caravans',
  'the-orchard-red-hill',
  'crittenden-villas',
];
const venues = slugs
  .map((slug) => allVenues.find((venue) => routeSlug(venue) === slug))
  .filter((venue): venue is NonNullable<typeof venue> => Boolean(venue));

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Stay', href: '/stay/' },
  { label: 'Dog-Friendly' },
];
export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Dog-Friendly Accommodation Mornington Peninsula · Peninsula Insider"
  description="Dog-friendly accommodation on the Mornington Peninsula - confirmed cottages, beach stays, and rural bases where the dog policy is real, not just a line in the listing."
  section="stay"
  canonical="https://peninsulainsider.com.au/journal/dog-friendly-accommodation-mornington-peninsula/"
  noindex={true}
  modifiedTime="2026-05-08"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />
  <article class="article">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="article__title">Dog-Friendly Accommodation on the Mornington Peninsula</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Dog-friendly stays on the Peninsula matter because the region's dog logic is uneven. Some beaches are off-leash, some are not. Some wineries welcome dogs at the cellar door, many do not. The right accommodation does more than permit a pet. It reduces friction across the whole weekend: fenced yards, direct beach access, space to leave the dog without guilt.</p>
        <p>The confirmed dog-welcoming properties are mostly self-contained cottages and rural bases. <a href="/stay/blue-moon-cottages/">Blue Moon Cottages</a> in Rye is 250 metres from the bay beach with a fenced courtyard in the Sandpiper unit and no extra pet fee. <a href="/stay/birch-creek/">Birch Creek</a> offers 40 acres near Red Hill for the dog who needs actual space. <a href="/stay/mp-beach-club-cottages/">MP Beach Club Cottages</a> are 200 metres from the bay at Tootgarook with private yards. <a href="/stay/kanasta-retro-caravans/">Kanasta Retro Caravans</a> at Rye takes dogs in designated vans for a nightly pet fee. <a href="/stay/the-orchard-red-hill/">The Orchard</a> at Red Hill South allows small dogs, with a pet fee, in the wine-country setting. <a href="/stay/crittenden-villas/">Crittenden Estate Villas</a> accommodate dogs subject to direct confirmation.</p>
        <p>Always confirm breed, size, and whether the dog can be left unattended at the property before booking. "Pet-friendly" in a listing is not a policy.</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--soft)">Last fact-verified: 8 May 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <section class="venues" id="rankings">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="venues__header">
        <div>
          <p class="label label--accent">Dog-friendly stays</p>
          <h2 class="venues__title">{venues.length} confirmed dog-welcoming bases on the Peninsula</h2>
          <p class="venues__sub">Properties where the dog policy is real - fenced yards, direct beach access, and space to actually be a dog.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/journal/dog-friendly-mornington-peninsula/" class="venues__link">Dog guide →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="venues__grid">{venues.map((venue) => <VenueCard venue={venue} hrefPrefix="/stay" />)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <NewsletterBlock />
</BaseLayout>
